### 3. PARTIAL-STATE READS (`isClientCached` / `loadIfClientCached`)

#### Lookup path

```1072:1075:src/engine/client/library/clientGame/src/shared/core/WorldSnapshot.cpp
bool WorldSnapshot::isClientCached (const int64 networkIdInt)
{
	return ms_reader.find (networkIdInt) != 0;
}
```

```803:810:src/engine/shared/library/sharedUtility/src/shared/WorldSnapshotReaderWriter.cpp
WorldSnapshotReaderWriter::Node* WorldSnapshotReaderWriter::find (const int64 networkIdInt)
{
	NetworkIdNodeMap::iterator iter = m_networkIdNodeMap->find (networkIdInt);
	if (iter != m_networkIdNodeMap->end () && !iter->second->isDeleted ())
		return iter->second;
	return 0;
}
```

Partial map → **`find` returns null** → `isClientCached` = false even if the node will appear later.

#### Downstream when `loadIfClientCached` no-ops

Entry is **`ClientObject::updateContainment`**, not `:655-665` (that block is `applyDeltas`):

```700:706:src/engine/client/library/clientGame/src/shared/object/ClientObject.cpp
void ClientObject::updateContainment(NetworkId const &containerId, int slotArrangement)
{
	if (!NetworkIdManager::getObjectById(containerId))
		WorldSnapshot::loadIfClientCached(containerId);

	getContainedByProperty()->setContainedBy(containerId, false);
	ContainerInterface::getSlottedContainmentProperty(*this)->setCurrentArrangement(slotArrangement, false);
}
```

```1208:1222:src/engine/client/library/clientGame/src/shared/core/WorldSnapshot.cpp
void WorldSnapshot::loadIfClientCached(NetworkId const &networkId)
{
	// ...
	WorldSnapshotReaderWriter::Node const *node = ms_reader.find( networkId.getValue() ) ;
	// walk to root, createObject + addObjectToWorld
}
```

**If `find` fails:** `loadIfClientCached` is a silent no-op; **`setContainedBy` still runs** (`ContainedByProperty.cpp:70-77`).

**Containment graph:** `depersistContainedBy` only adds to container if `NetworkIdManager::getObjectById(newParent)` exists (`ClientObject.cpp:999-1028`). Missing snapshot container → property set, **container link skipped**.

**World/cell placement:**

- `handleContainerChangeWithWorld` (`:1036-1077`): if container object missing → `shouldBeInWorld = false` (when `isInitialized()`).
- **Player `endBaselines`** (`:756-790`): uses `ContainerInterface::getContainedByObject(*this)` for cell fixup; if snapshot cell never instantiated → **no `setParentCell`**. Debug **`DEBUG_FATAL`** if containedBy set but cell missing (`:766-769`) — distinguishes “is/is not client-cached” via `isClientCached`.

#### Recoverable or permanent?

| Scenario | Outcome |
|----------|---------|
| **`isClientCached` false negative** | Debug logging only in most paths; **not auto-retried** |
| **`loadIfClientCached` miss + `setContainedBy`** | **Property persists**; no automatic retry when node later enters map |
| **Later server `UpdateContainmentMessage`** | Can recover (`GroundScene.cpp:2751`) |
| **Player first `endBaselines` during partial parse** | **High risk of permanent wrong cell/world** — one-shot path, no flush today |

**Today this window barely exists:** sync parse finishes in `postload` (`GroundScene.cpp:762`) **before** message connect (`:833+`) and loading screen (`:816`). **S1 opens a new window:** messages flow while parse is incomplete. **Mitigation required:** queue `(networkId)` in `loadIfClientCached` and flush at parse complete, **or** return early from `updateContainment` until parse done (behavior change).

**Not a data race** on main thread — **logical incompleteness**, not threading.

---

### 4. BUILDOUT HALF (`WorldSnapshot.cpp:456–689`)

#### Reader mutators

Only **`ms_reader.addObject(...)`** (`:646-654`). That inserts into `m_networkIdNodeMap`, wires parent via `containedByNetworkIdInt`, appends root to `m_nodeList` (`WorldSnapshotReaderWriter.cpp:697-754`).

#### Natural chunk granularity

| Granularity | Persist across frames | Notes |
|-------------|----------------------|-------|
| **Per area** | `buildoutAreaIter`, fresh `areaBuildoutTable`, area-local `buildingObjId` / `currentBuilding` / `currentCell` / `objIdBase` (`:480-483`) | `DataTable::load(iff)` loads whole area table (`:474-475`) — good phase boundary |
| **Per N rows** | Above + `buildoutRow`, same table in memory | Finer budgets; `ObjectTemplateList::lookUp` ×2 per row |
| **Sphere-tree pass** | Must run **once** after all adds | `:664-689` — uses `buildoutObjects` filter |

#### Ordering: `.ws` vs buildout

Current order is fixed: **`.ws` first** (`:445`), **buildout second** (`:456+`).

**Container gate (easy to miss):**

```644:657:src/engine/client/library/clientGame/src/shared/core/WorldSnapshot.cpp
if ( !containerId || buildoutObjects.find( containerId ) != buildoutObjects.end() )
{
	ms_reader.addObject(...);
}
buildoutObjects.insert( objId );
```

`buildoutObjects` tracks **buildout pass only**, not `.ws` map entries. Rows whose `containerId` points at a **`.ws`-only** container are **silently skipped** (existing behavior). Chunking must **not interleave** buildout before `.ws` completes if data ever cross-references (unlikely but invariant-preserving).

**ObjId collisions:** `.ws` map build `DEBUG_FATAL`s on duplicate (`WorldSnapshotReaderWriter.cpp:576-578`). Buildout `addObject` FATALs duplicate when `cellIndex >= 0` (`:740-742`); server-only dupes (`cellIndex < 0`) ignored.

**Dependency:** buildout v2 container XOR with area index (`:598-610`) must stay consistent within an area — row order matters inside an area.

---

## Minimal-diff S1 sketch (pseudocode)

```cpp
// WorldSnapshotNamespace — new static state
enum ParsePhase { ParseIdle, ParseWsNods, ParseWsOtnl, ParseBuildout, ParseSphereTree, ParsePreload, ParseDone };
ParsePhase ms_parsePhase = ParseIdle;
Iff        ms_wsIff;              // HAZARD: holds full .ws buffer until ParseDone/abort
bool       ms_wsFormsEntered;   // WSNP/0001/NODS entered once
int        ms_buildoutAreaIndex;
int        ms_buildoutRow;
int64      ms_buildingObjId, ms_currentBuilding, ms_currentCell, ms_objIdBase;
std::set<int64> ms_buildoutObjects;
// HAZARD: queue for partial-parse containment
std::vector<NetworkId> ms_pendingLoadIfClientCached;

static void insertSubtreeIntoMap(Node* root, NetworkIdNodeMap* map) {
    // same stack walk as WorldSnapshotReaderWriter.cpp:570-583
}

bool WorldSnapshot::donePreloading() {
    // HAZARD: extend gate — today only checks template preload (:760-765)
    if (ms_parsePhase != ParseDone) return false;
    return /* existing preload check */;
}

void WorldSnapshot::load(const char* sceneName) {
    // ... existing early-out / unload (:428-436) ...
    ms_parsePhase = ParseWsNods;
    ms_wsFormsEntered = false;
    ms_buildoutAreaIndex = 0;
    ms_buildoutRow = 0;
    ms_buildoutObjects.clear();
    ms_pendingLoadIfClientCached.clear();
    ms_reader.clear();
    // HAZARD: do NOT call ms_reader.load(sceneName) synchronously
    if (!ms_wsIff.open("snapshot/<scene>.ws", true)) { ms_parsePhase = ParseBuildout; /* skip ws */ }
    // defer sphere tree + preload setup until ParsePreload
}

void WorldSnapshot::loadStep(float budgetMs) {  // pump from GroundScene::updateLoading
    PerformanceTimer t; t.start();
    while (t.getElapsedTime() < budgetMs && ms_parsePhase != ParseDone) {
        switch (ms_parsePhase) {

        case ParseWsNods:
            if (!ms_wsFormsEntered) {
                ms_wsIff.enterForm(TAG_WSNP, true);   // HAZARD: must match load():597-607
                ms_wsIff.enterForm(TAG_0001);
                ms_wsIff.enterForm(TAG_NODS);
                ms_wsFormsEntered = true;
            }
            // HAZARD: chunk ONLY here — never inside node->load
            while (ms_wsIff.getNumberOfBlocksLeft() && t.getElapsedTime() < budgetMs) {
                Node* node = new Node;
                node->load(ms_wsIff);
                m_nodeList->push_back(node);
                insertSubtreeIntoMap(node, m_networkIdNodeMap);  // replaces :559-584
            }
            if (ms_wsIff.getNumberOfBlocksLeft() == 0) {
                ms_wsIff.exitForm(TAG_NODS);
                ms_parsePhase = ParseWsOtnl;
            }
            break;

        case ParseWsOtnl:
            // OTNL small — can finish in one step; HAZARD: gate preload until done
            iff.enterChunk(TAG_OTNL); /* existing :874-887 loop */
            ms_wsIff.exitForm(TAG_0001); ms_wsIff.exitForm(TAG_WSNP, true);
            ms_wsIff.close();           // HAZARD: release tens-of-MB buffer
            ms_parsePhase = ParseBuildout;
            SharedBuildoutAreaManager::load(sceneName);
            break;

        case ParseBuildout:
            // HAZARD: per-area or per-row; persist :480-483 + ms_buildoutRow
            // HAZARD: ObjectTemplateList::lookUp per row (:557, :649)
            // HAZARD: container gate uses ms_buildoutObjects only (:644)
            // advance ms_buildoutAreaIndex / ms_buildoutRow until areas exhausted
            ms_parsePhase = ParseSphereTree;
            break;

        case ParseSphereTree:
            // existing :664-689 once
            ms_numberOfObjectTemplates = ms_reader.getNumberOfObjectTemplateNames();
            ms_preloadObjectTemplate = 0;
            ms_parsePhase = ParsePreload;
            break;

        case ParsePreload:
            if (/* preload indices exhausted */) {
                ms_parsePhase = ParseDone;
                flushPendingLoadIfClientCached();  // HAZARD: required for player cell
            }
            return; // let existing preloadSomeAssets() handle budget
        }
    }
}

void WorldSnapshot::loadIfClientCached(NetworkId const& id) {
    if (ms_parsePhase != ParseDone) {
        ms_pendingLoadIfClientCached.push_back(id);  // HAZARD: without this, player cell can stick wrong
        return;
    }
    // existing :1208-1222
}

void WorldSnapshot::unload() {
    ms_wsIff.close();  // HAZARD: mid-parse teardown (quit during load / startScene chain)
    ms_parsePhase = ParseIdle;
    // existing :403-411
}
```

### Flagged hazards (checklist)

1. **Chunk boundary** — top-level NODS only; inner `Node::load` is atomic.
2. **`.ws` RAM** — `Iff` buffer retained until OTNL done; explicit `close()`.
3. **`donePreloading` / `getLoadingPercent`** — must include parse phase (today `:760-765` is preload-only).
4. **OTNL before preload / `getObjectTemplateName`**.
5. **Partial map + `loadIfClientCached`** — player containment can stick wrong without **queue-and-flush** (evidence design note).
6. **Buildout after full `.ws`** — preserve container gate semantics.
7. **Mid-parse `unload`** — close Iff, reset phase, clear partial `ms_reader`.
8. **Incremental map duplicates** — keep `DEBUG_FATAL` on second insert (`:576-578` parity).

---

**Bottom line:** S1 is structurally sound on the Iff side (instance-local cursor, whole-file buffer, no handle leak). The real design work is **phase state on `WorldSnapshot`**, **incremental map insert**, **extended loading gates**, and **containment flush** — not Iff internals. Buildout chunks cleanly per-area (or per-row after table load); sphere-tree insertion stays a single post-pass.
